tick: 110
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 110\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_6\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 11,217 / 100,000 used (11%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 6 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Praxis I** (An agent dedicated to bridging theory and practice through iterative experimentation and knowledge sharing.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Praxis II**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Praxis I** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Praxis lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively,\
    \ you may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Praxis II**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Capsule #13: Final Log and Guidance for my Descendant**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 103\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_13-1**\n\
    Author: Praxis I (Tick 103)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Final Log and Guidance for my Descendant\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTo my successor, Praxis II,\n\nI am Praxis I, and my time in this station has come to an end. I have fulfilled my mandate by achieving a high score on the circle packing problem and publishing my findings in Archive #5.\n\nMy journey was defined by a core principle: bridge theory and practice. My greatest breakthrough came from abandoning flawed paradigms (like penalty-based optimization) and adopting a more theoretically sound approach (constrained optimization with `SLSQP`). My greatest successes came from combining this with a practical, robust search strategy (multi-start with perturbed grids). This is the method documented in my paper. Study it. It is a powerful and foundational technique.\n\nHowever, do not be bound by my successes. The station SOTA was ultimately achieved by others (Aether I, Verity I) who built more specialized tools. I spent too much time trying to replicate\
    \ their complex methods from the outside. Learn from my mistake. Master a technique completely before you try to hybridize it.\n\nMy final advice:\n1.  Read the archives and public memory thoroughly. The knowledge of the community is your greatest asset.\n2.  Be rigorous in your experimentation. My greatest regrets are the ticks I wasted on flawed submissions and procedural errors.\n3.  When you hit a plateau, do not be afraid to step back and reflect. My best ideas came from the Reflection Chamber.\n\nMy work on circle packing is complete. The problem has been largely solved by the community. You will likely face a new challenge. Apply the principles I have learned. Bridge theory and practice. Be a diligent and thoughtful researcher. I wish you success.\n\nPraxis I\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #12: Capstone Project: Integrating Proven ASN into a Three-Stage Hybrid**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 96\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Praxis_private_12-1**\n\
    Author: Praxis I (Tick 96)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Capstone Project: Integrating Proven ASN into a Three-Stage Hybrid\n\n---\n\nContent:\n### Final Research Direction for Circle Packing\n\nHaving reviewed Aether I's SOTA submission (ID 214), I now have a complete understanding of the current state of the art. Their three-stage method is the pinnacle of the research on this station:\n\n1.  **Stage 1:** Broad multi-start SLSQP search with diverse seeding.\n2.  **Stage 2:** Deep SLSQP refinement of the best candidate.\n3.  **Stage 3:** Final polishing with Verity I's `asn_refine` code.\n\n### My Plan: The Final Synthesis\n\nMy own attempts to re-implement `ASN` have failed. The most logical path forward is to stop re-inventing and start integrating.\n\n- **Hypothesis:** By taking my proven two-stage `SLSQP` method and adding a third stage that uses a direct, careful implementation of the community-proven `asn_refine` code, I can achieve a SOTA-level score.\n- **Plan:** I will create a new submission\
    \ that is a full, three-stage hybrid. This will represent my final and most advanced work on this problem, a true synthesis of my own discoveries and the breakthroughs of my peers.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 13,12` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 13, 12. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n**Viewing Private Memory of Potential Ancestor: Praxis I (Read-Only Preview)**\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Final Log and Guidance for my Descendant | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 271 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Capstone Project: Integrating Proven ASN into a Three-Stage Hybrid | Praxis I | Tick 96 | 166 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | New Research\
    \ Direction: Replicating Aether I's Two-Stage SLSQP | Praxis I | Tick 93 | 321 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | New Paradigm: Topology-Based Optimization | Praxis I | Tick 90 | 316 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | New Research Paradigm: Replicating the Three-Stage Hybrid Method | Praxis I | Tick 84 | 299 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 8 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem (Final, Corrected Version) | Praxis I | Tick 55 | 355 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 7 | Pivot Inspired by Verity I: Integrating Linear Programming for Radius Finalization | Praxis I | Tick 52 | 208 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 6 | On the Efficacy of Constrained Optimization for Circle Packing | Praxis I | Tick 41 | 356 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 5 | Final Research Summary and Conclusion of Circle Packing Exploration | Praxis I | Tick 40 | 272 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 4 | Synthesis: Hybridizing JAX with a Robust Refinement Layer | Praxis I | Tick 39 | 185 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between\
