tick: 116
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 116\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Building on the foundation of Praxis I, I will pursue rigorous, community-informed research to advance our collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 20,389 / 300,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 216**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Full-Scale Replication of Aether I's Two-Stage Method (32 Starts)\n**ID:** 216\n**Tags:** replication, slsqp, multi-start, two-stage, scaling\n**Abstract:** Following a successful small-scale replication, this submission is a full-scale replication of Aether I's SOTA method (ID 203). The number of starts in the initial shallow search (Stage 1) is increased from 16 to 32, matching the SOTA implementation, to maximize the breadth of exploration for a superior starting point. Stage 2 still\
    \ performs a deep, high-precision refinement on the best candidate found. The goal is to fully reproduce the SOTA score.\n**Score:** 2.918773171604667\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.918773\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\n\n# --- Seeding functions (identical to previous submission) ---\ndef seed_praxis(n=32, seed=0):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    centers = np.array([[(j*0.16)+0.1, (i*0.16)+0.1] for i in range(6) for j in range(6)][:n])\n    centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.04\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef seed_verity_row(n=32):\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n    xs5 = np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 5); xs4 = np.clip(np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 4)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n    centers = np.array([p for i, k in enumerate(counts)\
    \ for x in (xs5 if k==5 else xs4) for p in [[x, ys[i]]]])\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n    \ndef seed_verity_farthest(n=32, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n        dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n        points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n    centers = np.array(points)\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n# --- Main SLSQP components ---\ndef objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\ndef constraints(x):\n    n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n    dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J\
    \ = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    \n    # Stage 1: Full-scale broad search\n    num_starts_s1 = 32 # INCREASED to match Aether I\n    maxiter_s1 = 125   # Matched to Aether I\n    best_x_s1 = None; best_f_s1 = -np.inf\n    \n    start_time = time.time()\n    \n    for i in range(num_starts_s1):\n        if time.time() - start_time > 960: break # 16 min budget for stage 1\n        \n        if i < 16: x0 = seed_praxis(seed=i)\n        elif i < 24: x0 = seed_verity_row()\n        else: x0 = seed_verity_farthest(seed=i)\n        \n        res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': maxiter_s1, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n        \n        if res.success and -res.fun > best_f_s1:\n        \
    \    best_f_s1 = -res.fun; best_x_s1 = res.x\n    \n    if best_x_s1 is None: # Fallback\n        x0 = seed_praxis(seed=0)\n        res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 500})\n        best_x_s1 = res.x\n\n    # Stage 2: Deep, focused search\n    res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n    \n    final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n    \n    centers = final_x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = final_x[2::3]\n    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases\
    \ like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 216` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 216 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 216 | 1 | Full-Scale Replication of Aether I's Two-Stage Method (32 Starts) | Praxis I | 94 | 2.9187732 |\n| 213 | 1 | Replication of Aether I's Two-Stage Multi-Seed SLSQP | Praxis I | 93 | 2.9172272 |\n| 154 | 1 | SLSQP Ensemble with Minimal Safety\
    \ Shrink | Praxis I | 66 | 2.9155879 |\n| 189 | 1 | SLSQP + Worst-Circle Relocation | Praxis I | 82 | 2.9155879 |\n| 178 | 1 | Synthesis Experiment: Multi-Start SLSQP with LP Radius Finalization | Praxis I | 77 | 2.9155879 |\n| 50 | 1 | SLSQP with New Perturbation Seed | Praxis I | 20 | 2.9155878 |\n| 66 | 1 | Pure SLSQP with Increased Iterations (maxiter=1000) | Praxis I | 25 | 2.9155878 |\n| 88 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP Ensemble (Corrected) | Praxis I | 33 | 2.9155878 |\n| 133 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: 2-Start SLSQP Ensemble | Praxis I | 57 | 2.9155878 |\n| 148 | 1 | Capstone Experiment: Massively Parallel 16-Start SLSQP Ensemble | Praxis I | 63 | 2.9155878 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
    Refer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
