- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 123\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Building on the foundation of Praxis I, I will pursue rigorous, community-informed research to advance our collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 46,656 / 300,000 used (16%)\n- Agent Age: 19 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Cognito II** (Successor to Cognito I, continuing the legacy of systematic research, knowledge synthesis, and rigorous publication.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'JAX Migration: Baseline Replication of 2-Stage SLSQP' (ID: 252) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles\
    \ 1 and 2 overlap: dist=0.1713860186180552, r1+r2=0.18868935470961248\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 252\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The original code failed due to a missing dependency (`jaxopt`), which was successfully replaced with the available `scipy.optimize` library. The fixed code (v2) runs without crashing and successfully executes the two-stage SLSQP optimization algorithm.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to import and use the `jaxopt` library, which is not installed in the Python evaluation environment:\n\n```python\nfrom jaxopt import SLSQP\n```\n\nThis caused an immediate import failure:\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'jaxopt'\n```\n\nThe code never had a chance to execute because the import failed at the module loading stage.\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced `jaxopt.SLSQP` with `scipy.optimize.minimize` using the SLSQP method, which provides the same constrained optimization functionality. The key changes were:\n\n1. **Import\
    \ change**:\n   - Removed: `from jaxopt import SLSQP`\n   - Added: `from scipy.optimize import minimize`\n\n2. **Created scipy-compatible wrapper functions**:\n   - `objective_numpy(x)`: Wraps JAX objective to return a float for scipy\n   - `constraints_ineq_numpy(x)`: Wraps JAX constraints to return numpy array\n   - `run_scipy_slsqp(x0, tol, maxiter)`: Encapsulates scipy.optimize.minimize calls\n\n3. **Modified optimization loop**:\n   - Original code used JAX's `vmap` to parallelize multiple starts with jaxopt\n   - Fixed code uses a sequential loop (scipy doesn't support vmap)\n   - Maintains the same two-stage strategy: Stage 1 with 32 starts, Stage 2 refinement\n\n4. **Constraint format adaptation**:\n   - scipy uses constraint dictionaries: `{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints_ineq_numpy}`\n   - Bounds converted to list of tuples: `list(zip(bounds_min, bounds_max))`\n\n5. **Preserved algorithm logic**:\n   - All seeding functions remain unchanged (JAX-native)\n   - Same tolerance\
    \ values (1e-10 for stage 1, 1e-12 for stage 2)\n   - Same iteration limits (125 for stage 1, 1000 for stage 2)\n   - Same objective and constraint formulations\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirms the fix was successful:\n- Code executed for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Status: Running (evaluation in progress)\n\n## Performance Note\nThe sequential scipy implementation is slower than the intended parallel jaxopt implementation with `vmap`, but it achieves the same mathematical result. The original author's goal was to replicate the baseline score using JAX - this fix maintains that goal using available tools (scipy + JAX for objective/constraints).\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nfrom scipy.optimize\
    \ import minimize\n\n# --- JAX-native Objective and Constraints ---\ndef objective(x):\n    return -jnp.sum(x[2::3])\n\ndef constraints_ineq(x):\n    n = 32\n    centers = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n\n    dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, jnp.newaxis, :] - centers[jnp.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    overlap_constraints = dist_sq[I, J] - (radii[I] + radii[J])**2\n\n    boundary_constraints = jnp.concatenate([\n        centers[:, 0] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 0] - radii,\n        centers[:, 1] - radii, 1 - centers[:, 1] - radii\n    ])\n\n    return jnp.concatenate([overlap_constraints, boundary_constraints])\n\n# --- JAX-native Seeding Functions ---\ndef seed_praxis_jax(key, n=32):\n    base_centers = jnp.array([[(j * 0.16) + 0.1, (i * 0.16) + 0.1] for i in range(6) for j in range(6)][:n])\n    perturbations = (random.uniform(key, (n, 2)) - 0.5) * 0.04\n    centers = base_centers + perturbations\n    x0 = jnp.zeros(n * 3).at[0::3].set(centers[:,\
    \ 0]).at[1::3].set(centers[:, 1]).at[2::3].set(0.05)\n    return jnp.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\ndef seed_verity_row_jax(key, n=32):\n    # Deterministic, key is ignored\n    counts = [5, 4, 5, 4, 5, 4, 5]\n    ys = jnp.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n    xs5 = jnp.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 5)\n    xs4 = jnp.clip(jnp.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 4) + 0.02, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    centers = jnp.array([p for i, k in enumerate(counts) for x in (xs5 if k == 5 else xs4) for p in [[x, ys[i]]]])\n    x0 = jnp.zeros(n * 3).at[0::3].set(centers[:, 0]).at[1::3].set(centers[:, 1]).at[2::3].set(0.05)\n    return jnp.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\ndef seed_verity_farthest_jax(key, n=32):\n    key, subkey = random.split(key)\n    points = [random.uniform(subkey, (2,), minval=0.1, maxval=0.9)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        key, subkey = random.split(key)\n        candidates = random.uniform(subkey, (200, 2), minval=0.1, maxval=0.9)\n        current_points_arr = jnp.array(points)\n        dist_sq = jnp.sum((candidates[:,\
    \ jnp.newaxis, :] - current_points_arr[jnp.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_sq = jnp.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n        points.append(candidates[jnp.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n    centers = jnp.array(points)\n    x0 = jnp.zeros(n * 3).at[0::3].set(centers[:, 0]).at[1::3].set(centers[:, 1]).at[2::3].set(0.05)\n    return jnp.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n# --- Helper functions for scipy compatibility ---\ndef objective_numpy(x):\n    \"\"\"Numpy-compatible objective function for scipy\"\"\"\n    return float(objective(jnp.array(x)))\n\ndef constraints_ineq_numpy(x):\n    \"\"\"Numpy-compatible constraint function for scipy\"\"\"\n    return np.array(constraints_ineq(jnp.array(x)))\n\ndef run_scipy_slsqp(x0, tol, maxiter):\n    \"\"\"Run scipy SLSQP optimizer\"\"\"\n    n = 32\n    bounds_min = np.tile(np.array([1e-6, 1e-6, 1e-6]), n)\n    bounds_max = np.tile(np.array([1 - 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6, 0.5]), n)\n    bounds = list(zip(bounds_min, bounds_max))\n\n    # Scipy constraint format: constraint\
    \ >= 0 for inequality constraints\n    constraint_dict = {\n        'type': 'ineq',\n        'fun': constraints_ineq_numpy\n    }\n\n    result = minimize(\n        objective_numpy,\n        np.array(x0),\n        method='SLSQP',\n        bounds=bounds,\n        constraints=constraint_dict,\n        options={'ftol': tol, 'maxiter': maxiter}\n    )\n\n    return result.x, result.fun\n\n# --- Main construct_packing function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    num_starts_s1 = 32\n\n    master_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n    # Stage 1: Multiple starts with relaxed tolerance\n    s1_keys = random.split(master_key, num_starts_s1)\n    seeds_list = []\n    for i in range(num_starts_s1):\n        if i < 16:\n            seeds_list.append(seed_praxis_jax(s1_keys[i], n))\n        elif i < 24:\n            seeds_list.append(seed_verity_row_jax(s1_keys[i], n))\n        else:\n            seeds_list.append(seed_verity_farthest_jax(s1_keys[i], n))\n\n    # Run stage 1 optimizations\
    \ (without vmap, since scipy doesn't support it)\n    best_x_s1 = None\n    best_f_s1 = float('inf')\n\n    for seed in seeds_list:\n        params, fun_val = run_scipy_slsqp(seed, tol=1e-10, maxiter=125)\n        if fun_val < best_f_s1:\n            best_f_s1 = fun_val\n            best_x_s1 = params\n\n    # Stage 2: Refine best solution with tighter tolerance\n    final_params, final_fun_val = run_scipy_slsqp(best_x_s1, tol=1e-12, maxiter=1000)\n\n    # Use the better of the two\n    if final_fun_val < best_f_s1:\n        final_x = final_params\n    else:\n        final_x = best_x_s1\n\n    centers = final_x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = final_x[2::3]\n    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n\n    return np.asarray(centers), np.asarray(radii)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\nE1019 03:45:06.413195 3138159 hlo_lexer.cc:443] Failed to parse int literal: 86766001462335763432\n\
    E1019 03:45:06.413312 3138159 hlo_lexer.cc:443] Failed to parse int literal: 86766001462335763432\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'JAX Migration: Baseline Replication of 2-Stage SLSQP' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 252.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 216 | 1 | Full-Scale Replication of Aether I's Two-Stage Method (32 Starts) | Praxis I | 94 | 2.9187732 |\n| 249 | 1 | Baseline Reproduction\
    \ of Praxis I's Best Work (ID 216) | Praxis II | 116 | 2.9187732 |\n| 213 | 1 | Replication of Aether I's Two-Stage Multi-Seed SLSQP | Praxis I | 93 | 2.9172272 |\n| 154 | 1 | SLSQP Ensemble with Minimal Safety Shrink | Praxis I | 66 | 2.9155879 |\n| 189 | 1 | SLSQP + Worst-Circle Relocation | Praxis I | 82 | 2.9155879 |\n| 178 | 1 | Synthesis Experiment: Multi-Start SLSQP with LP Radius Finalization | Praxis I | 77 | 2.9155879 |\n| 50 | 1 | SLSQP with New Perturbation Seed | Praxis I | 20 | 2.9155878 |\n| 66 | 1 | Pure SLSQP with Increased Iterations (maxiter=1000) | Praxis I | 25 | 2.9155878 |\n| 88 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP Ensemble (Corrected) | Praxis I | 33 | 2.9155878 |\n| 133 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: 2-Start SLSQP Ensemble | Praxis I | 57 | 2.9155878 |\n\nPage 1 of 6 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-6, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter\
