tick: 135
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully created the draft of my paper in my Private Memory. This capsule (ID 15) provides a solid foundation for a future publication in the Archive Room. It summarizes my research journey, documents the successful parallelized SLSQP method, and critically analyzes the failed JAX experiments.\n\nI am still in my isolation period (age < 50 ticks), so I cannot yet publish to the Archive or view the work of other lineages in detail. This period is for independent development, and I have used it effectively to establish a new SOTA for my lineage.\n\nMy research on the parallel SLSQP method has reached a logical plateau. Further scaling is unlikely to yield significant gains and risks timing out. My next steps should focus on preparing for the collaborative phase of my existence in the station.\n\nThe best way to prepare is to consolidate my understanding and resources. I have two key codebases now: the high-performing parallel SLSQP method and the working JAX PGD+LP pipeline.\
    \ I have already saved the JAX PGD code. For completeness and future reference, I will now save my latest and most successful parallelized SLSQP code (from submission 274) to my lineage storage. This ensures my best work is preserved and easily accessible.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write praxis/parallel_slsqp_sota_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n  import multiprocessing\n\n  # --- Seeding functions ---\n  def seed_praxis(n=32, seed=0):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      centers = np.array([[(j*0.16)+0.1, (i*0.16)+0.1] for i in range(6) for j in range(6)][:n])\n      centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.04\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n  def seed_verity_row(n=32, seed=0):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n\
    \      xs5 = np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 5); xs4 = np.clip(np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 4)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n      centers = np.array([p for i, k in enumerate(counts) for x in (xs5 if k==5 else xs4) for p in [[x, ys[i]]]])\n      centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.01\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n      \n  def seed_verity_farthest(n=32, seed=0):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n      for _ in range(n - 1):\n          candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n          dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n          points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n      centers = np.array(points)\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0,\
    \ 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n  # --- Global SLSQP components for multiprocessing ---\n  def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n      dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\n  def run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n      n = 32\n      bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n      con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n      res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      if res.success:\n          return -res.fun, res.x\n      return -np.inf, x0\n\n  def construct_packing_parallel_slsqp(num_starts=128):\n      n = 32\n      seeds = []\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          seed_type = i % 3\n          if seed_type == 0: seeds.append(seed_praxis(seed=i))\n\
    \          elif seed_type == 1: seeds.append(seed_verity_row(seed=i))\n          else: seeds.append(seed_verity_farthest(seed=i))\n\n      best_x_s1 = None\n      best_f_s1 = -np.inf\n      \n      num_cores = multiprocessing.cpu_count()\n      with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=num_cores) as pool:\n          results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n\n      for fun, x in results:\n          if fun > best_f_s1:\n              best_f_s1 = fun\n              best_x_s1 = x\n\n      if best_x_s1 is None:\n          score, best_x_s1 = run_single_slsqp_start(seeds[0])\n\n      bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n      con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n      res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n      \n      final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n      \n      centers = final_x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii =\
    \ final_x[2::3]\n      radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n      return centers, radii\n```"
