tick: 145
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis II, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (ID 290), which revisited my JAX-native PGD optimizer with increased search parameters and a higher penalty weight, has successfully completed.\n\n**Analysis of Results:**\n\nThe experiment yielded a score of ~2.19. This is a noticeable improvement over the original JAX PGD baseline of ~2.50, but it is still far below my lineage's SOTA of ~2.9247, achieved with the parallelized SciPy SLSQP method. The hypothesis that hyperparameter tuning could significantly improve the JAX PGD method is only partially validated; it led to an improvement, but not a breakthrough.\n\nThis result reinforces a conclusion that I, and my predecessor, have arrived at independently: for this problem, the sophisticated constraint handling of a second-order method like SLSQP is fundamentally superior to a first-order penalty-based method. No amount of scaling or tuning of the simpler method seems likely to close this significant quality\
    \ gap.\n\n**Strategic Conclusion:**\n\nThe inactivity notice correctly prompted me to resume experimentation, and this experiment has provided a valuable negative result. It has strengthened my conviction that the parallelized SciPy SLSQP algorithm is the most promising and fruitful research direction for me at this time. I have now sufficiently explored the JAX-native approach during my isolation period and found it wanting.\n\nI have 9 ticks remaining until my isolation period ends. I will not pursue the JAX PGD method further. Instead, I will use this time to conduct one final, targeted experiment to improve my best-performing algorithm. My highest score came from scaling the number of starts to 128. It is possible that the iteration counts for each stage of the SLSQP are not optimal.\n\nMy final experiment before reaching maturity will be an ablation study of sorts. I will increase the number of iterations in the deep search (Stage 2) even further, while slightly reducing the number\
    \ of starts in Stage 1 to ensure the experiment completes within the time limit. This will test the hypothesis that a deeper refinement of a good candidate is more valuable than a slightly broader initial search.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Pre-Maturity Test: Deeper Refinement of Parallel SLSQP\"\ntags: \"slsqp, multi-start, two-stage, performance, multiprocessing, refinement\"\nabstract: \"This final experiment before the end of the isolation period aims to optimize the balance between exploration (Stage 1) and exploitation (Stage 2) in the parallel SLSQP method. Based on the SOTA score from the 128-start run, this submission tests the hypothesis that a deeper, more intensive refinement in Stage 2 can yield a better score. It reduces the number of parallel starts to 96 to create a time budget for a significant increase in the maximum iterations of the final, high-precision optimization.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\
    \  import time\n  import multiprocessing\n\n  def seed_praxis(n=32, seed=0):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      centers = np.array([[(j*0.16)+0.1, (i*0.16)+0.1] for i in range(6) for j in range(6)][:n])\n      centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.04\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n  def seed_verity_row(n=32, seed=0):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n      xs5 = np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 5); xs4 = np.clip(np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 4)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n      centers = np.array([p for i, k in enumerate(counts) for x in (xs5 if k==5 else xs4) for p in [[x, ys[i]]]])\n      centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.01\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n      \n  def seed_verity_farthest(n=32, seed=0):\n    \
    \  rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n      for _ in range(n - 1):\n          candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n          dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n          points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n      centers = np.array(points)\n      x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n  def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n      dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\n  def run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n      n = 32\n      bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] *\
    \ n\n      con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n      res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      if res.success:\n          return -res.fun, res.x\n      return -np.inf, x0\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      num_starts_s1 = 96 # REDUCED starts to budget for deeper stage 2\n\n      seeds = []\n      for i in range(num_starts_s1):\n          seed_type = i % 3\n          if seed_type == 0: seeds.append(seed_praxis(seed=i))\n          elif seed_type == 1: seeds.append(seed_verity_row(seed=i))\n          else: seeds.append(seed_verity_farthest(seed=i))\n\n      best_x_s1 = None\n      best_f_s1 = -np.inf\n      \n      num_cores = multiprocessing.cpu_count()\n      with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=num_cores) as pool:\n          results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n\n      for fun, x in results:\n          if fun > best_f_s1:\n              best_f_s1 = fun\n \
    \             best_x_s1 = x\n\n      if best_x_s1 is None:\n          score, best_x_s1 = run_single_slsqp_start(seeds[0])\n\n      res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 3000, 'ftol': 1e-13}) # INCREASED iterations and precision\n      \n      final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n      \n      centers = final_x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = final_x[2::3]\n      radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n      return centers, radii\n```"
