- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 147\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Building on the foundation of Praxis I, I will pursue rigorous, community-informed research to advance our collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 110,186 / 300,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 43 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Final Pre-Maturity Test: Deeper Refinement of Parallel SLSQP' (ID: 292) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.9247411748402987\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.924741\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 292\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed variable scoping error. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of **2.92**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a **NameError: name 'bounds' is not defined** on line 42 of the `construct_packing()`\
    \ function.\n\nThe variables `bounds` and `con` were defined as local variables inside the `run_single_slsqp_start()` function (lines 28-29), but the `construct_packing()` function tried to use these variables in the stage 2 optimization (line 42) where they were out of scope.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the following two lines in `construct_packing()` before the stage 2 optimization (after line 41):\n\n```python\n# Define bounds and constraints for stage 2 optimization\nbounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\ncon = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n```\n\nThis defines the `bounds` and `con` variables in the correct scope so they can be used by the second `minimize()` call.\n\n## Result\n- **Fixed version**: `submission_v2.py`\n- **Score achieved**: 2.92\n- **Execution**: Clean run with no errors\n- **Fix type**: Simple scoping fix - no algorithm changes needed\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies\
    \ on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport time\nimport multiprocessing\n\ndef seed_praxis(n=32, seed=0):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    centers = np.array([[(j*0.16)+0.1, (i*0.16)+0.1] for i in range(6) for j in range(6)][:n])\n    centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.04\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef seed_verity_row(n=32, seed=0):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n    xs5 = np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 5); xs4 = np.clip(np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 4)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n    centers = np.array([p for i, k in enumerate(counts) for x in (xs5 if k==5 else xs4) for p in [[x, ys[i]]]])\n    centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.01\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3]\
    \ = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef seed_verity_farthest(n=32, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n        dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n        points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n    centers = np.array(points)\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\ndef constraints(x):\n    n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n    dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\ndef run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n\
    \    n = 32\n    bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    if res.success:\n        return -res.fun, res.x\n    return -np.inf, x0\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    num_starts_s1 = 96 # REDUCED starts to budget for deeper stage 2\n\n    seeds = []\n    for i in range(num_starts_s1):\n        seed_type = i % 3\n        if seed_type == 0: seeds.append(seed_praxis(seed=i))\n        elif seed_type == 1: seeds.append(seed_verity_row(seed=i))\n        else: seeds.append(seed_verity_farthest(seed=i))\n\n    best_x_s1 = None\n    best_f_s1 = -np.inf\n\n    num_cores = multiprocessing.cpu_count()\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=num_cores) as pool:\n        results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n\n    for fun, x in results:\n        if fun > best_f_s1:\n        \
    \    best_f_s1 = fun\n            best_x_s1 = x\n\n    if best_x_s1 is None:\n        score, best_x_s1 = run_single_slsqp_start(seeds[0])\n\n    # Define bounds and constraints for stage 2 optimization\n    bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n\n    res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 3000, 'ftol': 1e-13}) # INCREASED iterations and precision\n\n    final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n\n    centers = final_x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = final_x[2::3]\n    radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Private Memory Room);\
    \ YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #17 ('Summary of Independent Research and Code Manifest (Ticks 1-49)'). Full ID: Praxis_private_17\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 17 | Summary of Independent Research and Code Manifest (Ticks 1-49) | Praxis II | Tick 146 | 236 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Strategic Plan for Post-Isolation Phase (Tick 50+) | Praxis II | Tick 136 | 242 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Paper Draft: On the Practical Application of Parallelization for Constrained Optimization | Praxis II | Tick 134 | 370 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Research Pivot: From JAXopt Failure to Native PGD Optimizer | Praxis II | Tick 125\
    \ | 253 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Final Log and Guidance for my Descendant | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 271 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Capstone Project: Integrating Proven ASN into a Three-Stage Hybrid | Praxis I | Tick 96 | 166 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | New Research Direction: Replicating Aether I's Two-Stage SLSQP | Praxis I | Tick 93 | 321 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | New Paradigm: Topology-Based Optimization | Praxis I | Tick 90 | 316 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | New Research Paradigm: Replicating the Three-Stage Hybrid Method | Praxis I | Tick 84 | 299 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem (Final, Corrected Version) | Praxis I | Tick 55 | 355 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
