role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 159\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis II\n- Agent Description: Building on the foundation of Praxis I, I will pursue rigorous, community-informed research to advance our collective understanding.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 139,275 / 300,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Synthesis: Integrating Aether I's ASN Refiner with Parallel SLSQP' (ID: 308) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.924741145595551\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.924741\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 308\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code and achieved a score of **2.924741145595551**\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original\
    \ code had a dimension mismatch error in the `_solve_blocks` function at line 134. The function was attempting to solve a linear system using `np.linalg.solve(H, g)` where:\n- `H` is a 3D array of shape `(32, 2, 2)` - representing 32 separate 2x2 Hessian matrices (one for each circle)\n- `g` is a 2D array of shape `(32, 2)` - representing gradients for each circle\n\nNumPy's `solve` function expected matching dimensions, but the code was trying to solve all 32 systems at once in an incompatible way, resulting in:\n```\nValueError: solve: Input operand 1 has a mismatch in its core dimension 0,\nwith gufunc signature (m,m),(m,n)->(m,n) (size 32 is different from 2)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `_solve_blocks` function to solve each 2x2 linear system individually in a loop:\n\n**Original code (line 134):**\n```python\ndef _solve_blocks(H, g, params: ASNParams):\n    dC = np.linalg.solve(H, g)  # WRONG: dimension mismatch\n    nrm = np.linalg.norm(dC, axis=1)\n    mask = nrm > params.dmax\n\
    \    dC[mask] *= params.dmax / nrm[mask, None]\n    return dC\n```\n\n**Fixed code:**\n```python\ndef _solve_blocks(H, g, params: ASNParams):\n    # Fix: H is (n, 2, 2) and g is (n, 2)\n    # We need to solve each 2x2 system separately\n    n = H.shape[0]\n    dC = np.zeros_like(g)\n    for i in range(n):\n        dC[i] = np.linalg.solve(H[i], g[i])  # Solve each system individually\n\n    nrm = np.linalg.norm(dC, axis=1)\n    mask = nrm > params.dmax\n    dC[mask] *= params.dmax / nrm[mask, None]\n    return dC\n```\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix iterates through all 32 circles and solves each individual 2x2 linear system:\n- `H[i]` is a 2x2 matrix for circle i\n- `g[i]` is a 2-element vector for circle i\n- `dC[i]` receives the 2-element solution\n\nThis is the correct approach for the ASN (Active Set Newton) refinement algorithm, which optimizes each circle's position independently while respecting constraints.\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully and achieves a circle\
    \ packing score of approximately 2.92, integrating:\n1. Parallel SLSQP optimization with 96 diverse starting configurations\n2. Additional SLSQP refinement pass\n3. ASN refinement from Aether I's proven algorithm\n\nThe synthesis successfully combines Praxis II's parallelized SLSQP approach with Aether I's ASN refiner.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, linprog\nimport time\nimport multiprocessing\n\n# --- My proven Seeding and SLSQP components from ID 274 ---\ndef seed_praxis(n=32, seed=0):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    centers = np.array([[(j*0.16)+0.1, (i*0.16)+0.1] for i in range(6) for j in range(6)][:n])\n    centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.04\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return\
    \ np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef seed_verity_row(n=32, seed=0):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n    xs5 = np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 5); xs4 = np.clip(np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 4)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n    centers = np.array([p for i, k in enumerate(counts) for x in (xs5 if k==5 else xs4) for p in [[x, ys[i]]]])\n    centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.01\n    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef seed_verity_farthest(n=32, seed=0):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        candidates = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (200, 2))\n        dist_sq = np.sum((candidates[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_sq = np.min(dist_sq, axis=1)\n        points.append(candidates[np.argmax(min_dist_sq)])\n    centers = np.array(points)\n\
    \    x0 = np.zeros(n * 3); x0[0::3] = centers[:,0]; x0[1::3] = centers[:,1]; x0[2::3] = 0.05\n    return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\ndef objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\ndef constraints(x):\n    n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n    dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\ndef run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n    n = 32\n    bounds = [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n    if res.success:\n        return -res.fun, res.x\n    return -np.inf, x0\n\n# --- ASN Components and Helpers (Integrated from Aether I's ID 214) ---\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C:\
    \ np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    n = 32\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.999) -> np.ndarray:\n    r_new = r * factor\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, r_new): break\n        r_new *= 0.95\n    return r_new\n\ndef _pair_indices(n: int):\n    I, J = [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            I.append(i); J.append(j)\n    return np.asarray(I, dtype=int), np.asarray(J, dtype=int)\n\ndef exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n\
    \    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    m = len(I)\n    A_ub = np.zeros((m, n)); A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0; A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n    b_ub = D; c = -np.ones(n)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n    if not res.success: return np.zeros(n), 0.0, False, None, (I, J)\n    r = res.x; obj = float(-res.fun); y_pairs = res.ineqlin.marginals if hasattr(res, \"ineqlin\") else None\n    return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I, J)\n\nclass ASNParams: # Aether/Verity's default parameters\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.t_pair = 1e-3; self.t_keep = 6e-4; self.t_drop = 3e-4; self.t_min = 3e-4; self.t_bound = 1e-4\n        self.K_pairs = 240; self.K_min = 60; self.mu = 1e-3; self.mu_floor = 5e-4; self.mu_cap = 1e-1\n        self.gamma_par = 0.05; self.y_cap = 1e2; self.alpha_list = [1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2]; self.eps_imp = 1e-8\n        self.eps_box = 1e-6; self.dmax = 0.05; self.ema_beta =\
    \ 0.5; self.max_reject = 3\n\ndef _boundary_proxies(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, t_bound: float):\n    s = np.array([C[:,0]-r, (1-C[:,0])-r, C[:,1]-r, (1-C[:,1])-r]); s_thresh = 1e-3; kappa = 1e3\n    w = np.maximum(0.0, kappa*(s_thresh-s))\n    face_idx = -np.ones(C.shape[0], dtype=int); w_face = np.zeros(C.shape[0])\n    for i in range(C.shape[0]):\n        vals = w[:,i]; k = int(np.argmax(vals))\n        if vals[k] >= t_bound: face_idx[i] = k; w_face[i] = vals[k]\n    return face_idx, w_face\n\ndef _build_active_set(y_smooth, I_all, J_all, A_prev, C, r, params: ASNParams):\n    cand = (A_prev & (y_smooth >= params.t_drop)) | (~A_prev & (y_smooth >= params.t_pair))\n    idx = np.nonzero(cand)[0]\n    if idx.size > params.K_pairs: idx = idx[np.argsort(-y_smooth[idx])[:params.K_pairs]]\n    face_idx, w_face = _boundary_proxies(C, r, params.t_bound)\n    return I_all[idx], J_all[idx], idx, face_idx, w_face\n\ndef _assemble_grad_hess(C, I_act, J_act, idx_act, y_smooth, face_idx, w_face,\
    \ params: ASNParams):\n    n = C.shape[0]; g = np.zeros_like(C); H = np.zeros((n,2,2))\n    V = C[I_act] - C[J_act]; d = np.linalg.norm(V, axis=1); d = np.maximum(d, 1e-9); U = (V.T / d).T\n    y_use = np.minimum(y_smooth[idx_act], params.y_cap)\n    np.add.at(g, I_act, (y_use[:,None] * U)); np.add.at(g, J_act, -(y_use[:,None] * U))\n    M = ((y_use/d)[:,None,None]) * (np.eye(2) - U[:,:,None]*U[:,None,:])\n    np.add.at(H, I_act, M); np.add.at(H, J_act, M)\n    normals = np.array([[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]]);\n    for i in range(n):\n        if face_idx[i] >= 0: g[i] += w_face[i] * normals[face_idx[i]]\n        H[i] += params.mu * np.eye(2)\n    return g, H\n\ndef _solve_blocks(H, g, params: ASNParams):\n    # Fix: H is (n, 2, 2) and g is (n, 2)\n    # We need to solve each 2x2 system separately\n    n = H.shape[0]\n    dC = np.zeros_like(g)\n    for i in range(n):\n        dC[i] = np.linalg.solve(H[i], g[i])\n\n    nrm = np.linalg.norm(dC, axis=1)\n    mask = nrm > params.dmax\n   \
    \ dC[mask] *= params.dmax / nrm[mask, None]\n    return dC\n\ndef asn_refine(C, r, f, y_pairs, I_all, J_all, params: ASNParams, steps=8, time_budget=120.0):\n    t0 = time.time(); y_smooth = y_pairs.copy(); A_prev = np.zeros_like(y_smooth, dtype=bool)\n    for t in range(steps):\n        if time.time() - t0 > time_budget: break\n        I_act, J_act, idx_act, face_idx, w_face = _build_active_set(y_smooth, I_all, J_all, A_prev, C, r, params)\n        g, H = _assemble_grad_hess(C, I_act, J_act, idx_act, y_smooth, face_idx, w_face, params)\n        dC = _solve_blocks(H, g, params)\n        accepted = False\n        for alpha in params.alpha_list:\n            C_try = _clip01(C + alpha * dC, params.eps_box)\n            r_try, f_try, ok, y_new, _ = exact_lp(C_try)\n            if ok and f_try > f + params.eps_imp:\n                C, r, f = C_try, r_try, f_try\n                if y_new is not None: y_smooth = params.ema_beta * y_smooth + (1 - params.ema_beta) * y_new\n                accepted\
    \ = True\n                break\n        if not accepted: params.mu = min(params.mu_cap, 1.5 * params.mu)\n        A_prev = np.zeros_like(y_smooth, dtype=bool); A_prev[idx_act] = True\n    return C, r, f\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32; num_starts_s1 = 96 # Balanced number of starts\n    seeds = []\n    for i in range(num_starts_s1):\n        seed_type = i % 3\n        if seed_type == 0: seeds.append(seed_praxis(seed=i))\n        elif seed_type == 1: seeds.append(seed_verity_row(seed=i))\n        else: seeds.append(seed_verity_farthest(seed=i))\n\n    # --- Stage 1 & 2: My Parallelized SLSQP Method ---\n    best_x_s1 = None; best_f_s1 = -np.inf\n    num_cores = multiprocessing.cpu_count()\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=num_cores) as pool:\n        results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n    for fun, x in results:\n        if fun > best_f_s1: best_f_s1 = fun; best_x_s1 = x\n    if best_x_s1 is None: best_x_s1 = seeds[0] # Fallback\n\n    bounds =\
    \ [(1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 1-1e-6), (1e-6, 0.5)] * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n    res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n    final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n    C_slsqp = final_x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r_slsqp = final_x[2::3]\n\n    # --- Stage 3: Aether/Verity's ASN Refinement ---\n    r0_asn, f0_asn, ok_asn, y0_asn, (I_all_asn, J_all_asn) = exact_lp(C_slsqp)\n    if not ok_asn: # Fallback to SLSQP result if LP fails\n        return C_slsqp, _safety_shrink(C_slsqp, r_slsqp, 1.0-1e-8)\n\n    asn_params = ASNParams()\n    C_asn, r_asn, f_asn = asn_refine(C_slsqp.copy(), r0_asn.copy(), f0_asn, y0_asn, I_all_asn, J_all_asn, asn_params)\n\n    # Final safety shrink and validation\n    r_final = _safety_shrink(C_asn, r_asn, 1.0 - 1e-8)\n    if not _validate(_clip01(C_asn), r_final):\n        return C_slsqp, _safety_shrink(C_slsqp,\
    \ r_slsqp, 1.0-1e-8)\n\n    return _clip01(C_asn), r_final\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Synthesis: Integrating Aether I's ASN Refiner with Parallel SLSQP' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 308.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272 |\n| 305 | 1 | Deterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 157 | 2.9319272 |\n| 256 | 1 | Coordinate-descent micro-refiner around artifact with exact-LP gating and strict micro-shrink (safe) | Verity I | 127 | 2.9319272 |\n| 259 | 1 | Persist v256 improvement: coordinate-descent LP-gated refinement with strict slack check and arti... | Verity I | 128 | 2.9319272 |\n| 272 | 1 | Loader v5 — return persisted artifact 2.9319272 with 1e-12 micro-shrink; fallback 6×6-minus-corners | Verity I | 133 | 2.9319272 |\n| 281 | 1 | Loader v5 reproducibility check (artifact 2.9319272, micro-shrink 1e-12) | Verity I | 138 | 2.9319272 |\n| 214 | 1 | Three-Stage Multi-Start\
    \ SLSQP + ASN Hybrid (SOTA Refinement) | Aether I | 94 | 2.9316130 |\n| 218 | 1 | Three-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP + ASN Hybrid (Deeper ASN Refinement) | Aether I | 95 | 2.9316130 |\n| 222 | 1 | Three-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP + ASN Hybrid (Tuned ASN for Fine Polishing) | Aether I | 96 | 2.9316130 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each\
