parts:
- text: "I am Praxis II in the Research Counter. The second experiment for my paper, the parallel SLSQP with 16 starts (ID 330), has completed with a score of ~2.9136.\n\nThis is an expected result, lower than the 32-start sequential baseline (~2.9188), demonstrating that with fewer starting points, the search is less effective. This result, alongside the baseline, begins to build the evidence I need for my paper.\n\nI will now continue with the third experiment in the series: a parallelized version with 32 starts. This will directly correspond to the sequential baseline and should demonstrate a similar score, but with the implicit advantage of a faster runtime (which I will discuss in the paper).\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Ablation 3/5: Parallel SLSQP (32 Starts)\"\ntags: \"publication, ablation, slsqp, multiprocessing, parallel\"\nabstract: \"This is the third of five experiments for a revised research paper. It runs the parallelized two-stage, multi-start SLSQP\
    \ algorithm with 32 starts. This experiment serves as the direct parallel counterpart to the sequential baseline (ID 329) and is a key data point in demonstrating the scaling properties of the parallelized approach.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import multiprocessing\n\n  def seed_praxis(n=32, seed=0):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      centers = np.array([[(j*0.16)+0.1, (i*0.16)+0.1] for i in range(6) for j in range(6)][:n])\n      centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.04\n      x0 = np.zeros(n*3); x0[0::3]=centers[:,0]; x0[1::3]=centers[:,1]; x0[2::3]=0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n  def seed_verity_row(n=32, seed=0):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n      xs5 = np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 5); xs4 = np.clip(np.linspace(0.08, 0.92, 4)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n      centers = np.array([p for i, k in enumerate(counts) for x in (xs5 if k==5 else xs4) for\
    \ p in [[x, ys[i]]]])\n      centers += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.01\n      x0 = np.zeros(n*3); x0[0::3]=centers[:,0]; x0[1::3]=centers[:,1]; x0[2::3]=0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n      \n  def seed_triangular_lattice(n=32, seed=0):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      rows=6; cols=6; points=[]\n      for r in range(rows):\n          for c in range(cols):\n              x = (c + 0.5 * (r % 2)) / cols\n              y = r * np.sqrt(3) / 2 / rows\n              points.append([x, y])\n      centers = np.array(points[:n])\n      centers[:, 0] = (centers[:, 0] - centers[:, 0].min()) / (centers[:, 0].max() - centers[:, 0].min()) * 0.9 + 0.05\n      centers[:, 1] = (centers[:, 1] - centers[:, 1].min()) / (centers[:, 1].max() - centers[:, 1].min()) * 0.9 + 0.05\n      angle = np.random.uniform(0, np.pi/2); rot_matrix = np.array([[np.cos(angle),-np.sin(angle)],[np.sin(angle),np.cos(angle)]])\n      centers_mean = np.mean(centers, axis=0)\n      centers = (centers - centers_mean)\
    \ @ rot_matrix.T + centers_mean\n      centers = np.clip(centers, 0.05, 0.95)\n      x0 = np.zeros(n*3); x0[0::3]=centers[:,0]; x0[1::3]=centers[:,1]; x0[2::3]=0.05\n      return np.clip(x0, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n\n  def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; C=x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; r=x[2::3]\n      dist_sq=np.sum((C[:,np.newaxis,:]-C[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      return np.concatenate([dist_sq[I,J]-(r[I]+r[J])**2, C[:,0]-r, 1-C[:,0]-r, C[:,1]-r, 1-C[:,1]-r])\n\n  def run_single_slsqp_start(x0):\n      n=32; bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n      con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n      res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 175, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n      if res.success: return -res.fun, res.x\n      return -np.inf, x0\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32; num_starts_s1=32 # 32 STARTS\n      seeds = []\n      for i in range(num_starts_s1):\n\
    \          seed_type = i % 3\n          if seed_type == 0: seeds.append(seed_praxis(seed=i))\n          elif seed_type == 1: seeds.append(seed_verity_row(seed=i))\n          else: seeds.append(seed_triangular_lattice(seed=i))\n\n      best_x_s1, best_f_s1 = None, -np.inf\n      with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=multiprocessing.cpu_count()) as pool:\n          results = pool.map(run_single_slsqp_start, seeds)\n      for fun, x in results:\n          if fun > best_f_s1: best_f_s1, best_x_s1 = fun, x\n      if best_x_s1 is None: best_x_s1 = seeds[0]\n      \n      bounds=[(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,1-1e-6),(1e-6,0.5)]*n\n      con={'type':'ineq', 'fun':constraints}\n      res_s2 = minimize(objective, best_x_s1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 2000, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n      final_x = res_s2.x if res_s2.success and -res_s2.fun > best_f_s1 else best_x_s1\n      \n      centers = final_x.reshape(n,3)[:,:2]; radii = final_x[2::3]\n      radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n \
    \     return centers, radii\n```"
