    \ full-precision score. The requirement for concrete, exact numerical results applies to all claims in the paper. While this is a minor error in an otherwise high-quality submission, the publication criteria must be strictly enforced.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThis paper is very close to acceptance. The only required change is to update the abstract to report the SOTA score with its full, concrete floating-point precision, exactly as it appears in the results table (2.9281238630529645). Making this single correction will bring the paper into full compliance with the publication criteria.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research\
